---
title: Tabs
description: Tabbed content interface, with horizontal and vertical layout.
show_title: true
show_description: true
hide_table_of_contents: true
show_source: true
---

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-4">Standard variants</h2>
<p class="lead mx-3 my-4">Switch each tab set independently; compare horizontal and vertical layouts on mobile.</p>

{% set tab_content_1 %}
    <twig:block-text-image
        title="A clearer way to work together"
        content="Bring your team, information and everyday work together. Organize the details, share the context and keep the next action within reach. Clear information helps everyone follow the work and contribute at the right moment."
        :buttons="[
            {
                text: 'Learn more',
                url: 'https://www.example.com'
            },
            {
                text: 'Request a FREE trial period',
                url: 'https://www.example.com'
            }
        ]"
        image="assets/derafu-dev-programmer.png"
        :insideTabs="true"
    />
{% endset %}

{% set tab_content_2 %}
    <h2>Information</h2>
    <p>Bring your team, information and everyday work together. Organize the details, share the context and keep the next action within reach. Clear information helps everyone follow the work and contribute at the right moment....</p>
{% endset %}

<h3 class="h5 mx-3 mt-4">A continuous bar with five sections</h3>
<twig:block-tabs
    class="container my-4"
    :tabs="[
        {id: 'bar-workspace', title: 'Workspace', content: '<h3>Workspace</h3><p>Organize your everyday work.</p>'},
        {id: 'bar-connections', title: 'Connections', content: '<h3>Connections</h3><p>Connect the services your team uses.</p>'},
        {id: 'bar-reports', title: 'Reports', content: '<h3>Reports</h3><p>Explore the information behind your results.</p>'},
        {id: 'bar-documents', title: 'Documents', content: '<h3>Documents</h3><p>Keep shared documents within reach.</p>'},
        {id: 'bar-settings', title: 'Settings', content: '<h3>Settings</h3><p>Choose the settings for your workspace.</p>'}
    ]"
/>

<twig:block-tabs
    class="my-4"
    :tabs="[
        {
            id: 'features',
            title: 'Features',
            icon: 'fa-solid fa-list',
            content: tab_content_1
        },
        {
            id: 'info',
            title: 'Information',
            icon: 'fa-solid fa-info-circle',
            content: tab_content_2
        }
    ]"
/>

<twig:block-tabs
    class="my-4"
    position="vertical"
    :withShadow="true"
    :cols="3"
    :tabs="[
        {
            id: 'features2',
            title: 'hello',
            icon: 'fa-solid fa-list',
            content: tab_content_1
        },
        {
            id: 'info2',
            title: 'Information',
            icon: 'fa-solid fa-info-circle',
            content: tab_content_2
        }
    ]"
/>


<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Long content and layout checks</h2>
<twig:block-tabs
    class="container my-4"
    position="vertical"
    :cols="4"
    :tabs="[{id: 'long-tab-overview', title: 'Configuration and synchronization overview', content: '<h3>Overview</h3><p>A long navigation label should not reduce the content to a narrow column on mobile.</p>'}, {id: 'long-tab-details', title: 'Detailed instructions for the whole team', content: '<h3>Instructions</h3><p>The second panel remains independently selectable.</p>'}]"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Compact horizontal navigation from the theme</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Horizontal tabs fill the available width by default. This case keeps each tab close to its label width.</p>
<twig:block-tabs
    class="container my-4"
    style="--tab-horizontal-item-flex: 0 1 auto;"
    :tabs="[
        {id: 'compact-overview', title: 'Overview', content: '<h3>Overview</h3><p>A compact navigation can suit a small set of sections.</p>'},
        {id: 'compact-details', title: 'Details', content: '<h3>Details</h3><p>The panel uses the same content area as the default layout.</p>'}
    ]"
/>
